Description: fast, lightweight Linux system information fetch tool written in Rust
 KKFetch is a zero-runtime-dependency CLI system information fetch tool
 written in Rust, tailored for Linux systems. It gathers system specifications
 and displays them cleanly alongside distribution ASCII art logos with
 sub-millisecond execution performance and minimal resource overhead.
 .
 Features include:
  * Zero external runtime dependencies (native Linux kernel and /proc, /sys parsers)
  * Comprehensive metrics: CPU, GPU, Memory, Storage, Packages, Kernel, Desktop
  * Multi-distro ASCII art logos with ANSI 256-color support
  * Shell completions for Bash, Zsh, and Fish
